34: \section{Introduction}
35: 
36: Flow past a circular cylinder is one of the canonical problems in fluid mechanics. Measurements of cylinder drag span more than a century, from low-Reynolds-number experiments \cite{tritton1959} to high-Reynolds-number tests \cite{achenbach1968,roshko1961}. At Reynolds numbers between roughly $10^{3}$ and $2\times10^{5}$, the boundary layer remains laminar, separation occurs upstream of the shoulder, the wake is broad, and the drag coefficient is approximately constant at $C_D \approx 1.2$ \cite{schlichting2017,zdravkovich1997}. At higher Reynolds numbers, transition to a turbulent boundary layer delays separation, the wake narrows, and $C_D$ falls sharply to about 0.3 in the drag crisis \cite{roshko1961,achenbach1968}. The subcritical value is used in many engineering estimates, including offshore risers and moorings, towed arrays and cables, bridge piers, heat-exchanger tubes, and bluff-body wakes.
37: 
38: Most quantitative drag data for circular cylinders come from wind tunnels, where blockage, turbulence intensity and aspect ratio are relatively well controlled. Tow-tank measurements provide a complementary environment that is dynamically closer to marine applications, but they are affected by free-surface waves, carriage vibration, finite immersion and tank blockage. A reproducible tow-tank dataset at moderate Reynolds numbers is therefore useful both as a facility benchmark and as a baseline for more detailed wake and force measurements.
39: 
40: This paper documents a series of tow-tank measurements on three smooth circular cylinders with nominal diameters of 1, 1.5 and 2~in. The aims are (i) to report mean drag coefficients over $Re \approx 5\times10^{3}$--$5\times10^{4}$, (ii) to quantify the sensitivity of the results to water temperature and blockage, and (iii) to provide a reproducible dataset and processing workflow. The measurements are not intended to resolve the fine structure of the wake; rather, they establish a benchmark for the facility and a baseline for future work.
